                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2611.15844/2611.15844v1/cityscapes_vote_agreement_supp.png",
                "caption": "Figure 10:Vote agreement as a confidence estimate.OVB 9B withR=30R{=}30passes on the two Cityscapes images ofFig.7.Errors: pixels where the majority vote differs from the ground truth or is unassigned.Confidence estimate: vote agreement (Sec.D.2). Black: no ground truth. Errors and low agreement appear in the same places, mainly along object outlines and on small objects.",
                "position": 6069
            },
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2611.15844/2611.15844v1/geometry_nzs_comparison.png",
                "caption": "Figure 11:Paired zero-shot and non-zero-shot predictions.The 9B non-zero-shot model improves both NYUv2 examples, with less texture in the normal map. KITTI depth does not improve, and the ScanNet wall remains textured. Depth uses disparity-affine alignment and a shared color scale within each row (red near, blue far). White depth and gray normal regions mark invalid ground truth; predictions are shown without a validity overlay. Scores below predictions are per-image errors.",
                "position": 6307
            }
        ]
